MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Eagles felt like a natural next choice because their familiar, melodic classic rock fits the bluesy, roots-oriented music I want right now.",
    "Carole King and the Beatles also appealed through warm songwriting and memorable melodies, even though I would only choose the Eagles today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger, Death Magnetic and American Idiot share a broad rock connection with my listening, but their heavier metal or punk sound misses the bluesy feel I am seeking.",
    "Adele does not match my current interest in roots-oriented rock, while titles such as 25, Fallen and Partners leave me too uncertain about the music to choose them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Treating rock as one broad preference overlooks the difference between melodic, blues-influenced music and the metal or punk I passed over.",
    "Familiar album names alone are not enough to interest me when the sound does not fit what I want on this visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent listening points toward bluesy playing, roots-oriented rock and warm songwriting; those qualities matter more to me right now than a broad rock connection.",
    "An appealing suggestion does not always mean another choice: Carole King and the Beatles fit parts of my taste, but the Eagles satisfy my interest today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in classic songwriting but stretched it too broadly into heavier rock and music outside my current bluesy mood."
}
